# Compiled specs — versioned locally, never overwritten
docs/spec/compiled/

# Session logs and known issues
docs/ai/logs/

# Per-session governance verdict records (criteria verdicts). Same class as
# docs/ai/logs/ above: these are the TEMPLATE's own Critic/QA verdicts for
# TEMPLATE sessions, named by session uuid. They are meaningless in a child,
# they accumulate one file per session forever, and because they are tracked
# they entered the machinery manifest — so every regeneration churned the
# manifest and every sync delivered another template session's paperwork to
# every child. Excluded here rather than per-child so the file drops out of the
# manifest too, keeping sync and the withdrawn-file sweep reasoning about the
# same set (see t-0051, and the README note below for the same pattern).
docs/ai/governance/criteria-verdicts/

# Pristine-verification evidence (Decision t-0063). Hash-bound to ONE commit of
# the template's own enforcement mechanism, and one file is added per
# mechanism-change commit. Tracked, so each new one entered the machinery
# manifest: every mechanism change would have made the manifest stale the moment
# it was committed, and shipped a record about a template commit to every child
# where it can never match anything. A child's own evidence is written by its own
# commits and never appeared in a manifest, so the sweep cannot touch it. The one
# copy already shipped (t-0063-mechanism-change.yaml) is swept from a child only
# if a manifest that child received listed it; otherwise it is an inert orphan.
docs/ai/governance/pristine-evidence/

# .gitignore — excluded from generic file copy; merged via section markers
# in template-sync-engine.sh (BEGIN/END REPO-OS MANAGED block)
.gitignore

# A1 trigger index — GENERATED, and generated per-repo. The template's copy is
# built from the template's own decisions. Shipping it overwrote each child's
# index, and the A1 gate reads the index EXCLUSIVELY (pre-commit-gates.sh falls
# back to parsing decision files only when the index is ABSENT, which sync made
# impossible). Every child's own decisions were therefore unenforceable —
# markpreston had 22 of them. The sync engine now rebuilds the index in the
# child after syncing decisions instead of delivering the template's.
docs/ai/decisions/.a1-trigger-index

# Decision records: NOT excluded. Template decisions (`t-*`) sync to child repos.
# Child decisions (0100+) are safe — the sync engine operates add/update-only
# (does not delete child-only files), so project-specific decisions remain untouched.
# Orphaned template decisions are cleaned up via child-sync-decisions.sh using
# t-manifest.txt as the authoritative source (Decision 0022).

