docs/ai/knowledge-graph/product-graph.yaml
docs/ai/knowledge-graph/coverage.yaml

# Workflow files (repo-specific; GITHUB_TOKEN cannot push workflow changes)
#
# GitHub refuses a push from a GitHub App / GITHUB_TOKEN that creates or
# updates anything under .github/workflows/ without the `workflows` permission,
# which GITHUB_TOKEN cannot be granted (it is a PAT scope, not one of the
# workflow `permissions:` keys). Every workflow file added to this template
# MUST be listed here, or child sync fails at the push step with:
#   ! [remote rejected] main -> main (refusing to allow a GitHub App to
#     create or update workflow `...` without `workflows` permission)
# Children that want one of these run it by installing the file manually.
.github/workflows/template-sync.yml
.github/workflows/auto-version-tag.yml
.github/workflows/gate-conformance.yml

# Product README — a child's README describes the CHILD's product; the
# template's describes the template. Shipping ours replaced both children's
# product READMEs with "# Repo OS" on 2026-09-25, on a repo days from a public
# launch. Excluded here rather than claimed per-child so it also drops out of
# the machinery manifest, keeping sync and the withdrawn-file sweep reasoning
# about the same file set (see t-0051).
README.md

# A child's own claims (see _load_syncignore_patterns). Never synced: the whole
# point is that the child controls it, so delivering the template's copy would
# erase the claims on the sync that most needs them.
.templatesyncignore.local
